# Check text files out with LF on every OS (#5021). Tests compare testdata,
# generated tables and pack files byte for byte. On Windows, git's usual
# core.autocrlf=true checked them out with CRLF: on the first aial-04 run that
# failed psreader's generated-table check ("aliases_table.go is out of date with
# testdata\aliases") and the pack-content counts in mcp and policy. macOS and
# Linux clones are unchanged, because the files are LF already.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Captured from Windows PowerShell 5.1 with CRLF line endings, and compared
# byte for byte. Keep them exactly as committed.
internal/psreader/testdata/truth51/*.jsonl -text
